 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law and the state finance law, in relation to\nminority and women-owned business enterprise fraud and the monies of the\nminority and women-owned business enterprise fund; to amend a chapter of the\nlaws of 2022 amending the executive law and the state finance law relating to\nminority and women-owned business enterprises post completion certification,\nduties of the director and creating the minority and women-owned business\nenterprise fund, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 3390-A and A.\n9259-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; and to repeal certain\nprovisions of the executive law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S841",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S841-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §314-a, amd §§311 & 313, Exec L; amd §97-k, St Fin L; amd §6, Chap of 2022 (as proposed in S.3390-A & A.9259-A)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S841\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law and the state finance law, in relation\nto minority and women-owned business enterprise fraud and the monies of\nthe minority and women-owned business enterprise fund; to amend a chap-\nter of the laws of 2022 amending the executive law and the state finance\nlaw relating to minority and women-owned business enterprises post\ncompletion certification, duties of the director and creating the minor-\nity and women-owned business enterprise fund, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S. 3390-A and A. 9259-A, in relation to the effectiveness\nthereof; and to repeal certain provisions of the executive law relating\nthereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.567, to ensure trade secrets and other similarly private business\ninformation are kept confidential while still increasing transparency\nrequirements on MWBE license revocations and other final determinations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by requiring that deci-\nsions, revocations, and final determinations regarding the MWBE program\nwill be publicly-accessible information, while business trade secrets\nremain protected and confidential under the law. The Executive requested\nthis change due to the original bill's scope of information to be made\npublic.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 567 of the Laws of 2022. S.3390-A and\nA.9259-A both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June\n2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 relating to minority and women-owned busi-\nness enterprises post completion certification, duties of the director\nand creating the minority and women-owned business enterprise fund, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S.3390-A and A.9259-A.\n",
